@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Simple SysML Internal Block Diagram showing the interior of a HydraulicPump block.
'   usecase:      Teach parts (role:Type), connectors, ports, and the block interior view.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       fluid-power
' ============================================================================
title Example IBD - Simple Pump Interior

class "HydraulicPump" <<block>> {
}

package "HydraulicPump interior" {
  object "pMotor : Motor" as pMotor
  object "pChamber : PumpChamber" as pChamber
  object "pOutlet : OutletValve" as pOutlet

  port "HydraulicPump.inPwr" as inPwr
  port "HydraulicPump.outFlow" as outFlow
}

inPwr --> pMotor : power
pMotor --> pChamber : shaft
pChamber --> pOutlet : fluid
pOutlet --> outFlow : flow

note right of pMotor
  Each box is a PART (role:Type).
  The enclosing frame IS the block
  HydraulicPump; the parts compose it.
end note

note left of outFlow
  Boundary ports (inPwr, outFlow)
  are the block's interaction points
  visible from outside.
end note

@enduml
